  "before_interfaces": {
    "alg-composite-midpoint-rule": [
      "## Definition\n\nInput real numbers $a<b$, an integer $n\\ge1$, and a real-valued function\n$f:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb R$ evaluable at every point of $[a,b]$. Put\n$h=(b-a)/n$ and $m_j=a+(j+\\tfrac12)h$ for $0\\le j<n$. The composite midpoint\nrule returns\n\n$$Q_M(f;a,b,n):=h\\sum_{j<n} f(m_j).$$\n\nThe sum is the finite sum of [[def-finite-sum]]. The admissibility conditions\n$a<b$ and $n\\ge1$ ensure $h>0$ and all $m_j\\in(a+jh,a+(j+1)h)$. If an input\nfails either condition, the procedure returns invalid-grid; it makes no\nquadrature claim for that input. The rule is an exact-real formula; floating\npoint evaluation and summation error are separate from its quadrature error."
    ],
    "alg-composite-simpson-rule": [
      "## Definition\n\nInput real numbers $a<b$, an integer $n\\ge2$, and a real-valued function\n$f:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb R$ evaluable at every point of $[a,b]$. If $n$ is odd, the\nprocedure returns invalid-Simpson-panel-count. If $n$ is even, put\n$h=(b-a)/n$ and $x_j=a+jh$ for $0\\le j\\le n$; return\n\n$$Q_S(f;a,b,n):=\\frac h3\\sum_{j<n/2}\\bigl(f(x_{2j})+4f(x_{2j+1})+f(x_{2j+2})\\bigr).$$\n\nThe sum is a finite sum of [[def-finite-sum]]. Each two-panel block\n$[x_{2j},x_{2j+2}]$ uses its endpoints and midpoint. Expanding the block sum\ngives weights $1,4,2,\\ldots,4,1$. The even condition\n$n\\ge2$ makes the number of blocks a positive integer. If $a\\ge b$ or\n$n<2$, the procedure returns invalid-grid. The formula is an exact-real\nprocedure; floating point evaluation and summation error are separate from\nits quadrature error."
    ],
    "lem-composite-midpoint-panel-error-kernel": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $a<b$, $m=(a+b)/2$, and $f\\in C^2([a,b])$ in the sense of\n[[def-higher-derivatives-and-smoothness]]. Define\n\n$$K(t)=\\begin{cases}\\frac12(t-a)^2,&a\\le t\\le m,\\\\\\frac12(b-t)^2,&m\\le t\\le b.\\end{cases}$$\n\nThen $K$ is nonnegative and continuous,\n\n$$\\int_a^b f(t)\\,dt-(b-a)f(m)=\\int_a^b K(t)f''(t)\\,dt,$$\n\nand, with $M_2:=\\max_{t\\in[a,b]}|f''(t)|$,\n\n$$\\left|\\int_a^b f(t)\\,dt-(b-a)f(m)\\right|\\le\\frac{(b-a)^3}{24}M_2.$$\n\nIn particular, if $f''\\ge0$ on $[a,b]$, the panel midpoint value does not\nexceed the integral."
    ],
    "thm-composite-midpoint-error-bound": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $a<b$, let $n\\ge1$ be an integer, and put $h=(b-a)/n$. If\n$f\\in C^2([a,b])$, define $M_2=\\max_{x\\in[a,b]}|f''(x)|$. The composite\nmidpoint value $Q_M(f;a,b,n)$ of [[alg-composite-midpoint-rule]] satisfies\n\n$$\\left|\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx-Q_M(f;a,b,n)\\right|\\le\\frac{(b-a)h^2}{24}M_2.$$\n\nThe integral is the Riemann integral. This is an exact-arithmetic quadrature\nbound; evaluation and summation roundoff are not included."
    ],
    "lem-simpson-panel-peano-kernel": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $a<b$, put $L=b-a$ and $m=(a+b)/2$, and let $f\\in C^4([a,b])$. Define\nthe one-block Simpson value and its kernel by\n\n$$S(f;a,b):=\\frac{L}{6}\\bigl(f(a)+4f(m)+f(b)\\bigr),\\qquad K_{a,b}(x):=\\begin{cases}\\frac{(x-a)^3(3(x-a)-2L)}{72},&a\\le x\\le m,\\\\\\frac{(b-x)^3(3(b-x)-2L)}{72},&m\\le x\\le b.\\end{cases}$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx-S(f;a,b)=\\int_a^bK_{a,b}(x)f^{(4)}(x)\\,dx,$$\n\nand $K_{a,b}\\le0$ with\n$\\int_a^b|K_{a,b}(x)|\\,dx=L^5/2880$. The value $S(f;a,b)$ is the one-block\nspecialization of [[alg-composite-simpson-rule]]."
